  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Depression in freezing point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br />For one molal soloution ; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math> is least for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;; So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>&nbsp; is least but freezing point is high.</p>",
